dren's Fund (UNICEF) use data from administrative records and surveys reported annually by member states to estimate coverage\"},\n  {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"WHO has developed a model to estimate measles mortality in member states using numbers and age distribution of reported cases\"},\n  {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Compared with no measles vaccination, an estimated 15.6 million deaths were prevented by measles vaccination during 2000–2013\"},\n  {\"loc\": \"table 1\", \"q\": \"Any country not reporting data on measles cases for that year was removed from both the numerator and denominator.\"}\n ],\n \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}\n```", "type": "text"}]}